---
import Page from '../../components/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'about', n: 'What is this guide?' },
  { id: 'factors', n: 'Browse factors' },
  { id: 'chains', n: 'Browse chains' },
];
---

<Page
  pageTitle="Education hub"
  description="Background reading on DeFi risk, chains, evidence factors, and the exploits that shaped the rubric."
  crumbs={[{ n: 'Guide' }]}
  toc={toc}
  hero={{
    h1: 'Education hub',
    lede: 'Background reading on DeFi risk: how protocols fail, why the rubric is shaped the way it is, and what the evidence factors actually measure.',
  }}
>
  <h2 id="about">What is this guide? <a class="alink" href="#about">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    The rest of the site grades protocols. This section explains the vocabulary the grading uses
    so a reader who doesn't live in DeFi can still get value out of the dashboard.
  </p>

  <Callout kind="note" label="Work in progress">
    <p>
      This section is being built out. Content is being added progressively; check back for
      factor explainers, chain risk profiles, and background reading.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="factors">Browse factors <a class="alink" href="#factors">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    Each of the 184 evidence factors has a methodology page covering what we look for, why it
    matters, and how scoring breaks down. Start with the
    <a class="link" href="/factors/">factor encyclopedia</a> for the full index.
  </p>

  <h2 id="chains">Browse chains <a class="alink" href="#chains">#</a></h2>
  <p>
    Each chain hosts protocols with different risk profiles. The chain pages summarize which
    protocols we've graded on each chain and what the typical risk pattern looks like.
  </p>

</Page>
